    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/graph/propositions/@N003/statement",
      "value": "ell has integer image λ and ell<p; n=ell+1>0. T is a nonzero finite-dimensional K-vector space with dimension n. For every natural r≤ell, (r! as a scalar in K)≠0. Each c_j (j∈I) and C has nonzero image in K. The endomorphisms F of T satisfy, for all i,j,k,l∈I, F_ij F_kl=F_il when j=k and are zero otherwise, and ∑_{i∈I} F_ii=Id_T. Scalar extension hat preserves addition, integer scalar multiplication, composition, identity, finite sums and powers. For r≤ell, X̂_r=(r! as a scalar in K)^{-1}x̂^r and Ŷ_r=(r! as a scalar in K)^{-1}ŷ^r; ĥ=x̂ŷ−ŷx̂. For every f0∈End_ℤ(M), α0∈K and m0∈M, hat(f0)(α0⊗m0)=α0⊗f0(m0)."
